1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,900
Ladies and gentlemen,

2
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,240
Amtrak is happy to announce our arrival in New York City.

3
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,774
The train will be stopping in five minutes.

4
00:00:06,774 --> 00:00:09,150
Please check to be sure you have your belongings.

5
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:11,912
And have a good stay in the Big Apple.

6
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:13,112
Thank you.

7
00:00:13,112 --> 00:00:14,890
Well, here we are.

8
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:17,868
It was so nice meeting you, Mr.Stewart.

9
00:00:17,868 --> 00:00:20,846
And nice meeting you, too, Mrs.Tobin.

10
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:21,930
Please look us up.

11
00:00:21,930 --> 00:00:23,824
We're in the phone book.

12
00:00:23,824 --> 00:00:26,802
Dr. Philip Stewart, in Riverdale.

13
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:27,802
Your son?

14
00:00:27,802 --> 00:00:32,758
That's right. And have a good time in New York.

15
00:00:32,758 --> 00:00:34,758
And don't be so independent.

16
00:00:34,758 --> 00:00:50,625
You're very lucky to have a caring family.

17
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:53,225
When can we go fishing?

18
00:00:53,225 --> 00:00:54,696
Robbie, we'll go fishing soon,

19
00:00:54,696 --> 00:00:56,581
and we'll take your dad with us.

20
00:00:56,581 --> 00:01:03,992
I'm ready, Grandpa. You name the day.

21
00:01:03,992 --> 00:01:05,355
That's a great idea, Grandpa!

22
00:01:05,355 --> 00:01:05,555
Philip needs a day off.

23
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:07,615
Let's give him our presents--now.

24
00:01:07,615 --> 00:01:08,493
Good idea.

25
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:14,449
Presents--for me?

26
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:16,449
From me and Marilyn.

27
00:01:16,449 --> 00:01:17,427
And this one's from me.

28
00:01:17,427 --> 00:01:35,295
I looked all over the house to find it.

29
00:01:35,295 --> 00:01:39,623
Richard, these are terrific pictures.

30
00:01:39,623 --> 00:01:50,915
This one really brings back memories.

31
00:01:50,915 --> 00:01:54,496
You remember that day, Robbie?

32
00:01:54,496 --> 00:01:59,118
I sure do. It was fun.

33
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:08,034
Oh, I'm sorry Susan isn't here.

34
00:02:08,034 --> 00:02:10,052
I miss her very much.

35
00:02:10,052 --> 00:02:11,670
She feels bad, too, Grandpa.

36
00:02:11,670 --> 00:02:14,437
She called to say the plane was delayed.

37
00:02:14,437 --> 00:02:15,722
You know airports.

38
00:02:15,722 --> 00:02:18,126
I can't wait to see her.

39
00:02:18,126 --> 00:02:22,154
She looks just like Grandma at that age.

40
00:02:22,154 --> 00:02:24,942
I'd better unpack.

41
00:02:24,942 --> 00:02:29,178
I started traveling twenty-four hours ago.

42
00:02:29,178 --> 00:02:33,676
I'm not so young anymore.

43
00:02:33,676 --> 00:02:37,832
Don't you want something to eat?

44
00:02:37,832 --> 00:02:40,810
No, thanks.

45
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:43,788
After a good night's sleep, I'll enjoy breakfast even more.

46
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:45,112
Well, come on, Dad.

47
00:02:45,112 --> 00:02:47,866
Ellen and I'll take you to your room.

48
00:02:47,866 --> 00:02:49,744
I'm sure glad you're here, Grandpa.

49
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:51,424
Good night, Grandpa.

50
00:02:51,424 --> 00:02:55,362
Pleasant dreams.

51
00:02:55,362 --> 00:03:10,589
Philip, do you have the key to the trunk?

52
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:13,567
I have the key, but it doesn't work.

53
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:22,723
I sent the wrong key.

54
00:03:22,723 --> 00:03:38,391
I have something for you. I made it myself.

55
00:03:38,391 --> 00:03:43,347
I think you'll enjoy it.

56
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:46,325
I researched it for over a year.

57
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:52,281
It's our family tree.

58
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:57,259
Oh, Grandpa! How exciting!

59
00:03:57,259 --> 00:03:58,237
Fabulous!

60
00:03:58,237 --> 00:04:03,215
Why, I didn't know that your grandfather was born in Germany.

61
00:04:03,215 --> 00:04:05,793
Lots of interesting information about our family.

62
00:04:05,793 --> 00:04:10,149
A gift from me.

63
00:04:10,149 --> 00:04:16,105
Thank you so much.

64
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:16,772
Grandpa! Grandpa!

65
00:04:16,772 --> 00:04:21,483
Oh, Grandpa, I'm so happy to see you!

66
00:04:21,483 --> 00:04:26,538
Oh, you look so beautiful, Susan. My granddaughter.

67
00:04:26,538 --> 00:04:30,994
Like I always said, you look just like Grandma.

68
00:04:30,994 --> 00:04:33,972
I think you're going to be very happy here with us.

69
00:04:33,972 --> 00:04:36,950
I know you will.

70
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:39,950
I don't feel alone anymore.
